  "notes": "No cry, ruins or bodies drawn. Light for «برحمة» after Shu'ayb's name (94:5). 94:4-10 is not glossed (first person). STAGING v4: Madyan's town by day, as in 11_90-93. c1 (94): Shu'ayb (blue drop labelled Shu'ayb) and three believers (light robes; three is the series' sign for a group) stand in the town while the rescue is told; a soft sparkle on the believers for We saved (94:4); no close-up while Shu'ayb's name is recited and repeated (94:5). They leave the stage together on 94:9, the word of mercy (the believer group fades in place, the drop to its side), with a geometric plate for mercy from Us (94:9-10; not a light plate on a pronoun of Allah): they leave on a word of rescue, more than 3 s before the punishment is named (94:11). No departure route or destination is drawn (the tafsirs give none). The wrongdoers are never drawn: the blast (94:14) falls on the empty town by day (not dawn), no body, no ruin. c2 (95): the empty town; a leaf plate and drifting leaves for as though they had never lived there (95:1-4); the camera drifts over the empty street for away with Madyan as Thamud went away (95:5-10). Cover: the empty town with the leaf plate (the end of Madyan)."
